{
  "id": 477361718,
  "iid": 24570,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "http-urlencoded: fix percent-decoding bounds check",
  "description": "Fix off-by-one in percent-decoding bounds check in packet-http-urlencoded.c.\n\nA valid percent-escape requires two hex digits after '%', so at least 3 bytes (\"%xx\") must be available. The previous check only required 2, which allowed incomplete escapes like \"%A\" at the end of a field.\n\nThis updates the check from \\< 2 to \\< 3 while preserving the existing TVB exception handling for truncated packets.\n\nTested with sample captures and a minimal PoC:\n\n- x=%41 decodes to \"A\"\n- x=%A is treated as an incomplete escape",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2026-04-23T21:42:39.125Z",
