  "discussions_data": [
    {
      "id": "cc00082ce4e0d5d04629c965f80b7295286b0cb7",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3281414944,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> Using reported length for parsing can lead to over-read or incorrect behavior when packets are truncated (reported > captured). This change ensures all operations are safely bounded by captured data.\n\nNo, I believe the current operations all call the TVB API functions like `tvb_memcpy` that do bounds checking and throw appropriate exceptions on truncated packets. We want that to happen.\n\nPlease provide a PoC of captures that you believe are currently being dissected incorrectly.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-04-23T22:03:00.640Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-04-23T22:03:53.733Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 477361718,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 24570,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "5ef8e4379cfcf21818d829911e102c1b9652ff22",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3283274953,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Thanks for the feedback.\n\nYou're right that the TVB APIs (e.g., tvb_memcpy) perform bounds checking and will throw exceptions on truncated packets. My intent here was not to replace that safety mechanism, but to ensure that parsing logic itself does not rely on reported length for control flow.\n\nIn the previous code, tvb_reported_length_remaining() and tvb_reported_length() were used to:\n\n- determine loop bounds\n- compute lengths for parsing\n- drive offset progression\n\nIn cases where reported length exceeds captured length, this can lead to:\n\n- parsing decisions being made based on bytes that are not actually present\n- offsets advancing past the captured buffer before an exception is triggered\n\nThe updated approach ensures that:\n\n- all parsing decisions are based on captured data\n- offsets never advance beyond tvb_captured_length()\n- malformed or truncated inputs are handled consistently without relying on exceptions for control flow\n\nThat said, I understand your point that TVB exceptions already provide safety. If preferred, I can narrow the scope of this change to only the clearly problematic paths (such as the percent-decoding bounds check), or provide a more concrete example where reported-length-based control flow leads to undesirable parsing behavior.\n\nI will work on constructing a minimal PoC capture to better demonstrate the behavioral difference.",
          "author": {
            "id": 31060610,
            "username": "urvalkheni",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Urval Kheni",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/31060610/avatar.png?v=1788515628",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/urvalkheni"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-04-24T09:17:48.977Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-04-24T09:17:48.977Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 477361718,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
