    {
      "id": "e62608eb38620af414a6bd836cfcbe59ed017cf3",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3287435982,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> offsets never advance beyond tvb_captured_length()\n\nThis is not a problem, so long as the API is used, which throws exceptions.\n\n> malformed or truncated inputs are handled consistently without relying on exceptions for control flow\n\nSorry, we want to rely on exceptions for control flow. If a packet is truncated we want to throw a `BoundsError`, which adds an item to the tree automatically for `[Packet size limited during capture...`, unless it's marked as fragmented, in which case the item about it being a fragment is added.\n\nIt's possible to check and throw the correct exception manually instead, but that's often more work and more prone to errors.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
