        {
          "id": 3287478384,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I’ve dropped the broader reported-vs-captured parsing changes and kept only the percent-decoding bounds fix.\n\nThe remaining change updates the check from \\< 2 to \\< 3 for \"%xx\", ensuring incomplete percent-escapes (e.g., \"%A\" at the end of a field) are handled correctly, while still relying on the standard TVB exceptions for truncated packets.\n\nI also tested this with a minimal PoC:\n\n- Valid case: `x=%41` -\\> `Form item: \"x\" = \"A\"`\n- Invalid case: `x=%A` -\\> `Form item: \"x\"` with no decoded value\n\nThis demonstrates the incomplete percent-escape case addressed by the updated bounds check.",
