        {
          "id": 3305350624,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Thanks for sharing these PCAPs.\n\nThe real topic here is not really about _truncated_ packets, which are handled correctly, but about abnormal data which looks to be percent-encoded but which isn't exactly. The way it is currently handled helps triggering a `Malformed Packet Exception`, which is a desirable behavior, which your suggestion would remove.",
