        {
          "id": 3309436677,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Thanks for the feedback.\n\nI've updated the patch to use tvb_ensure_bytes_exist(tvb, offset, 3) instead of returning false. This preserves the expected exception-based handling for malformed or truncated percent-escapes.\n\nWith this change:\n\n- x=%41 decodes correctly\n- x=%A now triggers a \"Malformed Packet\" as expected\n\nLet me know if this aligns with expectations.",
